From 8d7e9c08611238f5bba7757072c16018c1a83d02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:03:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace invented catalogue with verified published research

Every resource, supplement and diagnostic entry was fabricated: invented
authors, institutions and dates, backed by 20 placeholder PDFs that only
said "Placeholder document". Presented as a citable library on a mental
health site, that risked people citing studies that do not exist. The
"Milton & Fen-Hollande Research Group" attribution was the worst case,
attaching a fake study to a real autism researcher.

The catalogue is now built entirely from real publications, each checked
against publisher and PubMed records for title, authors, journal,
volume/issue, pages and DOI:

- Milton (2012) double empathy; Murray, Lesser & Lawson (2005)
  monotropism; Crompton et al. (2020) autistic peer-to-peer transfer
- Raymaker et al. (2020) autistic burnout; Newson et al. (2003) PDA
- Faraone et al. (2021) World Federation of ADHD consensus statement
- Quadt, Critchley & Garfinkel (2018) interoception
- Reis, Baum & Burke (2014) twice-exceptional definition
- Diagnostics: Arns et al. (2013) EEG, Jones & Klin (2013) eye-tracking,
  Ecker et al. (2015) MRI, Demontis et al. (2019) ADHD genetics
- Supplements: Bloch & Qawasmi (2011) omega-3, Wang et al. (2017) iron,
  and a zinc dose-response meta-analysis

Entries now link out to the DOI rather than redistributing papers we have
no licence to host, with free full text flagged where it exists.
downloadUrl stays supported but optional, for documents the site may
lawfully host; all placeholder PDFs are deleted.

Claims are written to match what the studies actually found, including
where they are negative: the EEG entry now records that theta/beta ratio
was judged unreliable as a diagnostic, rather than implying otherwise.

Modalities and supplements without a verifiable source (CPT, digital
phenotyping, magnesium, vitamin D, L-theanine) are removed rather than
kept on unsourced claims.

